# Prepared caller clock Source proposal

This immutable proposal supplies the missing authored caller lifecycle for
ordinary manual and legacy run-period thermal steps. It contains nine changed
existing Rust files and two new Rust files. No canonical source was changed and
no formatter, compiler, project test, engine or scientific output was used.

`CtfHistoryCallerClock` is a distinct owner in `HeatBalanceState`, allocated by
the actual ordinary initializer. Its flags begin true and its committed count
begins zero. The actual warmup/run loops supply their phase/day/hour request,
zone substep, steps/hour and duration. Preparing retains a pending stamp;
committing clears the first flags only after the real thermal return succeeds.
Neither clock construction nor its commit reads the surface timestep counter,
coefficient timestep or a Native observation.

Warmup uses its existing typed retained-failure check after the void callback.
The shared run-period driver commits only after its Result returns Ok and the
same retained-failure check succeeds. An error keeps the pending clock, count
and first flags; another attempt cannot replay that step. No failed caller
return refreshes producer authority or records a completed thermal step.

The shared loop covers standalone heat balance and the actual coupled
PurchasedAir run-period caller. Its predictor-hook signature and existing
temperature/humidity/history/report ordering remain intact. This proposal adds
clock preparation before that hook and caller commit before output collection.
It does not change the purchased-air `begin_environment` operand.

Production weather remains authoritative: the presence of an owned Production
context selects that context's actual clock, including genuine unavailable
None. The legacy caller never supplies a replacement for Production. Legacy
dry-bulb and Legacy weather-series paths use the actual prepared loop clock.

The new public `advance_heat_balance_state_one_timestep_with_clock` returns
Result and invokes the existing source-order body once. An ordinary manual
caller can own `CtfHistoryCallerClock`, call prepare with explicit caller
operands, pass that stamp to the fallible entry and commit only after Ok. The
existing three-argument void entry supplies no clock; ordinary ownership still
retains its honest MissingCallerClock error. No implicit fallback is added.

The compile-time producer witness list adds the actual clock/timestep/caller
sources and production weather source. It continues to use literal include_str
bytes without runtime filesystem I/O, custom digest or dependency. No existing
generation primitive, public coefficient or consumer-view check is weakened.

Three new tests use the real ordinary massive construction initializer with
authored Zone/Space membership: two distinct manual steps/weather values,
actual legacy warmup-to-run loops sharing one first-environment lifecycle, and
an actual material mutation which fails before commit and cannot replay.
Their expectations concern ownership, clocks and successful calls, with no
calculated expected temperatures or Native endpoint values. The fixture body
is copied exactly from the existing lifecycle test model, recorded separately.
The tests are unexecuted Source proposals.

Existing lifecycle/math tests and the separate Base fixture/empty-layout fixes
are untouched. Before refs are the actual current formatted activation Source;
the manifest records the actual formatted inventory membership where present.
Root must merge any independently accepted concurrent parent changes, perform
FULL source review and obtain an independent peer before applying this package.
Broader interzone/material admission, diagnostics, physics assertions, Native
whole-runtime evidence and CTF gates are unchanged by this proposal.
